{
 "captions": [
  {
   "at": 1521,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore"
   ],
   "text": "A second program, run from reset: point x1 at 0x50000000, load from it, store what came back to RAM A, then jump there. Device 5 does not exist on this chip."
  },
  {
   "at": 1713,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore",
    "tp_bus"
   ],
   "text": "The load enters MEM with dmem_addr = 0x50000000. tp_bus sees that no device decodes it and answers at once with 0, so the core leaves MEM on the next clock."
  },
  {
   "at": 1858,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore",
    "tp_bus"
   ],
   "text": "jalr x0, 0(x1): the core fetches from 0x50000000. The bus answers this fetch at once too, with the all-zero word."
  },
  {
   "at": 1873,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore"
   ],
   "text": "All zeros is not a RISC-V instruction, so ILLEGAL (uo_out[6]) rises and stays high. From the pins you can see that something went wrong; the chip keeps running."
  },
  {
   "at": 1914,
   "blocks": [
    "tp_ncore",
    "qspi_ctrl"
   ],
   "text": "Reset clears ILLEGAL; the core returns to FETCH and the memory wake-up starts again."
  }
 ],
 "checks": [
  {
   "ok": true,
   "text": "a load from 0x5000_0000 is answered within one pass (no stall in MEM)"
  },
  {
   "ok": true,
   "text": "the load reads 0: stored over 0x22222221 in RAM A"
  },
  {
   "ok": true,
   "text": "jumping to 0x5000_0000 fetches 0: ILLEGAL rises, no HALT"
  },
  {
   "ok": true,
   "text": "reset recovers: FETCH, memory wake-up restarts"
  }
 ],
